{"id":"ibleam","name":"Ibleam","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ibleam"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ibleam","text":"People-waster, a city assigned to Manasseh (Josh. 17:11), from which the Israelites, however, could not expel the Canaanites (Judg. 1:27). It is also called Bileam (1 Chr. 6:70). It was probably the modern Jelamah, a village 2 1/2 miles north of Jenin."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2991","lemma":"יִבְלְעָם","xlit":"Yiblᵉʻâm","gloss":"Jibleam, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Ibleam","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H4023","lemma":"מְגִדּוֹן","xlit":"Mᵉgiddôwn","gloss":"Megiddon or Megiddo, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Megiddo, Megiddon","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H1756","lemma":"דּוֹר","xlit":"Dôwr","gloss":"Dor, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Dor","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H8590","lemma":"תַּעֲנָךְ","xlit":"Taʻănâk","gloss":"Taanak or Tanak, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Taanach, Tanach","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H1052","lemma":"בֵּית שְׁאָן","xlit":"Bêyth Shᵉʼân","gloss":"Beth-Shean or Beth-Shan, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Beth-shean, Beth-Shan","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","xlit":"Mᵉnashsheh","gloss":"Menashsheh, a grandson of Jacob, also the tribe descende","kjv":"Manasseh","count":2,"share":0.67}],"verses":["Josh.17.11","Judg.1.27","2Kgs.9.27"],"related":[{"id":"megiddo","type":"lexical","strong":"H4023","why":"both lead with מְגִדּוֹן (H4023)"},{"id":"taanach","type":"lexical","strong":"H4023","why":"both lead with מְגִדּוֹן (H4023)"}],"works":[]}
